# Sales Dashboard

A **page** is a `.work` file that's mostly **prose** with a few embedded units that
**render by default** — declared data, an island, an image. Markdown narrates; the
units run. Nothing here is a mock-up.

## A board from declared tasks

Declare `Task` values and they render as a board. `owner` must resolve to a real
person or agent; `ref` points at the unit the task is about — both checked at the
weave gate.

data :board, of: Task, from: values([
  %Task{title: "Backfill enrichment", status: :doing, owner: :priya, ref: :enrich},
  %Task{title: "Tune scoring weights", status: :doing, owner: :dana,  ref: :score},
  %Task{title: "Draft outreach for Initech", status: :todo, owner: :analyst, ref: :analyst}
])

This is **live state**, not a snapshot — the document *is* the store. The same values
power the [[Plan]] page's full view.

## An island

A `client` unit is an island: it hydrates in the browser, so it works even in the
static bundle. Pass it a typed value rather than letting it fetch.

client svelte :chart do
  <script>
    export let leads = [];
    $: ranked = [...leads].sort((a, b) => b.score - a.score);
    $: max = Math.max(1, ...ranked.map((l) => l.score));
  </script>

  {#each ranked as lead}
    <div class="row" class:hot={lead.score >= 80}>
      <span>{lead.name}</span>
      <div class="bar" style="width: {(lead.score / max) * 100}%">{lead.score}</div>
    </div>
  {/each}
end

A page ships three ways with no rewrite — static bundle, nexus SSR, live SSR (see
[[Deploy]]). Next: [[Styling a workbook]].
